WEBVTT

1

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.120

Hey. Answer the damn

question, you twit.



2

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.540

What do you want to do?



3

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.750

I want to join the Scouts...



4

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.700

...and slaughter every Titan I can!



5

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.830

Ah. Not bad.



6

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:44.000

Erwin. I'll take

responsibility for him.



7

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.500

Let the higher-ups know.



8

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.620

I don't necessarily

trust him, though.



9

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.040

If he betrays us

or goes out of control,



10

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.790

I'll kill him on the spot.



11

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:57.000

The top brass won't complain.



12

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.200

Because I'm the only

one cut out for this.



13

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.160

You're in.



14

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.120

I'll make you a

member of the Scouts.



15

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:40.620

<i>I won't let your deaths be meaningless</i>



16

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:46.750

<i>even if I'm the last one standing</i>



17

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.620

<i>In both hands, Gloria</i>



18

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.620

<i>What sings is Sieg</i>



19

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:02.870

<i>On my back, Flügel der Freiheit</i>



20

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:09.700

<i>Clenched determination to my left chest</i>



21

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:15.040

<i>What slashes across is Linie der Torheit</i>



22

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.290

<i>Soaring across the azure skies</i>



23

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.830

<i>Flügel der Freiheit</i>



24

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:41.290

"Can't Look into His Eyes Yet"

"Eve of the Counterattack, Part 1"



25

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:00.080

Hey, is it true that a

Titan sided with humans?



26

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.330

That's obviously just a rumor.



27

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.040

I bet the recapture plan failed



28

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.540

and loads of people from

Wall Rose are gonna flee here.



29

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.500

"Interior of Wall Sina"



30

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.580

If that happens, we'll have

food shortages in no time flat.



31

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.290

Man, please tell me

those Wall Rose people



32

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:20.750

aren't gonna show up here

with this Titan friend of theirs...



33

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.830

"Wall Sina"

"Wall Rose"



34

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.200

This is huge news!



35

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.330

"Interior of Wall Rose"

We have a Titan on our side now!



36

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:33.120

Who knows, maybe we

can even retake Wall Maria!



37

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.000

It's almost like it's... it's...



38

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.580

...our savior!



39

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.000

Oh!



40

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.160

Savior, huh?



41

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.790

Throughout history, commoners

have always been a rash lot.



42

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.450

I can see this triggering a

revolt against the central powers...



43

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:59.870

Not if we, the Military Police,

dispose of Eren Jaeger first.



44

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.790

I won't let those Scout

Regiment deviants have him.



45

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.290

Fall in!



46

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.160

Hail to the Premier!



47

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.660

It's certainly hot.



48

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.160

Commander Pyxis.



49

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.660

You're the top commander

of the Garrison Regiment



50

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.620

and I'm a commanding officer

of the Scout Regiment.



51

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.870

Won't some disapprove of

us meeting like this?



52

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:39.370

Oh, you're as straight-laced

as the rumors say.



53

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.950

Still, this is just a morning walk.



54

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.120

We only met by happenstance.



55

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:50.040

So, let's chat during our little stroll.



56

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.040

Have you heard that the Military Police



57

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.830

wants to take custody of Eren Jaeger?



58

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.160

Yes, I received word yesterday.



59

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.660

They're going to hold

a deliberation on the matter.



60

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:01.660

Mm.



61

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.950

It falls entirely

to Zachary to decide



62

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:09.370

whether the Scouts get him

or the Military Police gets him.



63

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.000

Zachary...



64

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.950

You mean Premier Dhalis Zachary?



65

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.660

He oversees the three regiments:



66

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:20.790

the Military Police, the Garrison

Regiment, and the Scouts.



67

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.620

He will base his decision on one thing:



68

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:28.370

whether his existence is

beneficial or harmful for humanity.



69

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:33.120

If he deems him a detriment, he won't

hesitate to have Eren executed.



70

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.830

Right there, on the spot, even.



71

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.120

I don't want them to kill Eren.



72

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.790

But, unfortunately,

many in the Garrison Regiment



73

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:46.410

are fearful of Eren's ability.



74

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:52.250

The most I can do is avoid

agreeing with the Military Police.



75

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.830

Are the odds in your favor?



76

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.250

No.



77

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.410

But we <i>do </i>have a proposal ready.



78

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.040

Whether or not it'll work depends

on how the debate unfolds.



79

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.870

You'll be playing it entirely

by ear, in other words?



80

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.200

Our line of work

takes us outside the walls.



81

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.000

We always play things by ear.



82

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.620

It seems you're

not so uptight after all.



83

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:25.250

This has been a nice walk,

Commander Smith.



84

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.200

A debate over Eren?



85

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.200

What for?



86

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.700

I'm not really sure,



87

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.000

but I think it's about

what they plan to do with him.



88

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.750

What do you mean?



89

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.540

My guess...



90

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.950

...is they're going to decide

if he should live or die...



91

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:53.080

Are Mikasa Ackermann

and Armin Arlelt here?!



92

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.700

Yes!



93

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:59.000

You are ordered to attend this

afternoon's deliberation as witnesses!



94

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.250

Excuse me! I need to use the toilet...



95

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.870

You just went!



96

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:14.410

Please give me some water!



97

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.830

Hey!



98

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:20.120

Know your place, monster.



99

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.160

Monster...



100

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:28.370

Yeah, that might be the case...



101

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.500

But am I so terrifying that

I need to be restrained this much?



102

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.790

I guess I can't blame them, though.



103

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:39.250

Even I don't understand any of this.



104

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:43.580

At least they haven't killed me yet...



105

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.370

Come to think of it,



106

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:51.950

<i>they </i>weren't afraid of me at all.



107

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.790

What are they doing now?



108

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:03.700

What happened to all the others?



109

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:10.450

Just hang on a little longer.



110

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.830

We'll try to arrange things somehow.



111

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:16.580

How many days has it been since then?



112

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.200

What's going on on the outside?



113

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.410

I'm... not going to spend the

rest of my life in here, am I?



114

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.950

So you're Eren, huh?



115

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.370

You okay? How are things?



116

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.830

I'm sorry you've had to wait so long.



117

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.410

But now you have a

chance to finally get out.



118

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.370

Except...



119

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:48.790

...you'll have to put these on.



120

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:57.790

I'm Hange Zoë, a section

commander in the Scout Regiment.



121

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:00.950

And this is Miche Zacharius,

also a section commander.



122

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:02.660

U-Umm...



123

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:08.540

Oh, he always sniffs people like

that when he first meets them.



124

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.870

He has a habit of

laughing through his nose.



125

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:13.830

I doubt he means anything by it.



126

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:18.120

Oddness aside, he <i>is </i>skilled enough

to be a section commander.



127

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.580

Oops!



128

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.200

Sorry! I just prattled on, didn't I?



129

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.160

We're already here, but...



130

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.160

No, it'll be okay!



131

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.620

It's actually better if I don't explain!



132

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.040

W-Wait...!



133

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:39.950

It's selfish of us, but all we

can do is put blind faith in you.



134

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.500

--Good luck!

--Huh?!



135

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:58.040

A courthouse?



136

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:01.870

I was in the basement of a courthouse?



137

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.290

Get moving!



138

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:15.700

Kneel down!



139

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.500

What's with all these people?



140

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.450

In fact, what is this trial even about?!



141

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.000

Guys!



142

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.040

Shall we begin?



143

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.410

You are Eren Jaeger,



144

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:57.290

a soldier who has sworn

to give his life for the people.



145

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.950

Is that correct?



146

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.410

Yes.



147

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.290

Given the extraordinary circumstances,



148

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:04.370

this deliberation will be held

as a court-martial;



149

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.910

regular law will not apply,

in other words.



150

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:11.330

I have full decision-making

authority in this matter,



151

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:15.660

which includes determining

whether you should live or die.



152

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.250

Just as I thought!



153

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.910

Any objections?



154

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:21.790

No, Sir.



155

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:24.200

Your astuteness is appreciated.



156

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:26.540

I'll get right to the point.



157

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:31.290

As expected, concealing your

existence has proved impossible.



158

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:35.120

Unless we publicly disclose your

existence in one fashion or another



159

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:38.950

we risk the outbreak

of a new, non-Titan threat.



160

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:44.700

It falls to me to decide which

regiment should take charge of you.



161

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.950

The Military Police Regiment...



162

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:48.700

Or the Scout Regiment...



163

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:53.160

Now let's hear what the

Military Police Regiment proposes.



164

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.160

Yes, Sir.



165

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.160

I, Nile Dawk, Commander

of the Military Police,



166

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.790

offer the following proposal.



167

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:03.580

We believe that, after a thorough

examination of Eren's body,



168

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:06.450

he should be disposed of immediately.



169

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:13.160

It's true that his Titan ability

helped thwart this latest incursion.



170

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:19.040

However, his existence is now

stirring up rebellious ideas as well.



171

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:23.370

As such, after he's provided us

with as much information as possible,



172

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:27.000

he will be made a

fallen warrior of humanity.



173

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.120

There's no need!



174

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.580

He is vermin that

has defiled and infiltrated



175

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.790

--...the walls built by God's great wisdom!

--He's with the Wall cult!



176

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:37.040

--He should be killed at once!

--Everyone ignored them five years ago...



177

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:40.450

--Pastor Nick. Please remain quiet.

--...but they've really grown in power.



178

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:44.250

Next, let us hear the Scout Regiment's idea.



179

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.830

Yes, Sir.



180

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:49.250

I, Erwin Smith, 13th Commander

of the Scout Regiment,



181

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.660

offer the following proposal.



182

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:56.250

We intend to accept Eren as an

official member of the Scout Regiment



183

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:59.790

and utilize his Titan

ability to retake Wall Maria.



184

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.410

That is all.



185

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:07.120

Hmm? That's all?



186

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:08.450

Yes, Sir.



187

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:12.160

With his help, we <i>can </i>reclaim Wall Maria.



188

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:15.700

I believe it is clear what

our utmost priority should be.



189

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.370

I see.



190

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:22.580

Tell me, from where

would you launch this operation?



191

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:23.790

Pyxis.



192

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:27.870

The wall has been completely

sealed in Trost District, correct?



193

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.120

Yes.



194

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.330

I doubt its gate will ever open again.



195

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.500

We hope to depart from

Calaneth District, to the east.



196

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.160

From there we would

approach Shiganshina



197

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.620

by establishing a

new route from scratch.



198

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.250

Just a damn minute!



199

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:45.500

Shouldn't we be

sealing <i>all </i>the gates now?!



200

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:49.160

The gates are the only part

the Colossal Titan can break!



201

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.910

If we can just reinforce them,

we'll never get attacked again!



202

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:55.200

Shut up, you merchant dog!



203

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.330

With a Titan's help

we can return to Wall Maria!



204

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:03.370

We can't put up with any more of

your childish heroics!



205

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:05.410

You have a big mouth on you, swine.



206

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.290

What guarantee is there



207

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.700

that the Titans will kindly

wait while we bolster the gates?



208

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.660

When you say "we",

you mean the friends you're protecting



209

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.660

so you can fatten yourselves up.



210

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:21.160

Are you pigs blind to the people



211

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.200

who struggle to survive

off what little land is left?



212

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:28.620

I'm just saying that all we have to

do is seal the gates if we want to live!



213

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:31.750

Hold your tongue, you miscreant!



214

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:33.620

You would suggest



215

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:37.080

that humans meddle with

Wall Rose, a gift from God?!



216

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:41.120

That wall is a divine miracle that

transcends human understanding!



217

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.120

--Do you still not realize...

--It's their fault...



218

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:46.410

--...that humanity must not touch it!

--...it took so long to arm the tops of the walls.



219

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:49.370

They have that much support and power now.



220

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.250

They're a bad sort.



221

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:52.450

Th-That's disrespectful!



222

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.750

Shut it, you lousy priest!



223

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.160

What?!



224

00:14:58.540 --> 00:14:59.790

Order!



225

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:04.160

I ask that you save your personal

sentiments for another venue.



226

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:07.290

I wish to make certain

of something, Mr. Jaeger.



227

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:11.120

As a soldier, can you

continue to serve humanity



228

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.830

by controlling your Titan ability?



229

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.000

Yes, Sir! I can!



230

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.250

Oh?



231

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:22.500

But it says here in this

report about the Trost battle



232

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:27.620

that just after transforming, you swung

your fists at Mikasa Ackermann.



233

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:33.450

He doesn't remember

that he wasn't in control...



234

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.160

What, you expect me to lie in a report?



235

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.910

Hiding this fact wouldn't do

humanity any good.



236

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.700

And who is Mikasa Ackermann?



237

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:45.000

I am, Sir.



238

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.540

You, huh?



239

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.790

Is it true that Jaeger,

in Titan form, attacked you?



240

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:56.200

It's in Eren's best interest

that you answer honestly.



241

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.950

Yes. It's true.



242

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:08.620

I knew it! A Titan's a Titan!



243

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:11.580

I tried to kill Mikasa?!



244

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.000

<i>Me</i>?!



245

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:14.950

However...



246

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:21.040

He also saved my life on two

prior occasions while in Titan form.



247

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.540

The first time,



248

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.540

just as I was about to

fall into the hands of a Titan,



249

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:30.040

he intervened and protected me.



250

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:37.000

The second time, he protected

Armin and me from a bombardment.



251

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.410

I ask that you take these facts

into consideration as well.



252

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:42.500

Just a minute!



253

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.500

I believe that her testimony



254

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.450

is also very driven by personal feelings.



255

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:51.750

It should be noted that Mikasa Ackermann

lost her parents at a young age



256

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:54.830

and was taken in by the Jaeger family.



257

00:16:56.410 --> 00:17:00.040

What's more, our own

investigation into this matter



258

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.410

led us to a most surprising discovery.



259

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.370

Eren Jaeger and Mikasa Ackermann,

at the age of nine,



260

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:11.950

stabbed and killed

three adult robber-kidnappers.



261

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:15.660

Even if it <i>was </i>in self-defense,



262

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:19.830

we cannot help but

question his basic humanity.



263

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.540

Should we <i>really </i>place

personnel and funds in his hands,



264

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:26.410

not to mention the very fate of humanity?!



265

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:27.580

Yeah!



266

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:31.120

He's clearly a Titan that's snuck

in by taking the form of a child!



267

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:32.540

Her too!



268

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:35.120

I bet she's not human at all!



269

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:38.120

Yeah! We should

dissect her just to be safe!



270

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.540

Hold on!



271

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:43.120

I might be a monster,

but she has nothing to do with this!



272

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.290

Nothing at all!



273

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.450

--Like we can believe you!

--It's the truth!



274

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.910

--She <i>is </i>one if you hafta protect her!

--No!



275

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:56.620

No... It's not like that.



276

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:03.580

But you're all using speculation

to push your own selfish agendas!



277

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:06.000

Wh-What?!



278

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.580

In fact...



279

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:08.580

Is this bad?



280

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:13.000

...none of you have even <i>seen</i>

a Titan, so why are you so afraid?!



281

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.000

Maybe I should stop talking...



282

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:20.200

No, I'm gonna tell 'em

<i>everything </i>I think!



283

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:25.330

What's the use of having power

if you're not going to fight?!



284

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:30.410

If you're afraid of fighting for

your lives, then help me!



285

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:33.000

You... cowards!



286

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:33.750

What?



287

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.700

Just shut up...



288

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:38.160

...and invest everything in me!



289

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:44.620

Take aim!



290

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:46.040

Yes, Sir!



291

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.450

Huh?



292

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.200

Wait, Mikasa!



293

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.580

My personal belief



294

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.910

is that <i>pain </i>is the best tool

for teaching discipline.



295

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:18.410

What you need now



296

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:21.620

is to be taught a lesson,

not given a talking-to.



297

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:25.160

And you happen to be

in perfect kicking position.



298

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:37.410

Wait, Levi!



299

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:38.830

What?



300

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:41.830

That's dangerous.



301

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:45.250

What if he gets mad

and turns into a Titan?



302

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.910

Don't be silly.



303

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:53.450

<i>You </i>guys are gonna

dissect him, aren't you?



304

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:57.410

When he was transformed,



305

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:00.790

he apparently managed to kill twenty

Titans before running out of strength.



306

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:06.120

As an enemy, his intelligence

makes him all the more dangerous.



307

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:09.450

Even so, I could handle him just fine.



308

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.040

But could you?



309

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:15.450

Whoever dares to torment

him had better think long and hard.



310

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:17.750

<i>Can </i>you actually kill him?



311

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:21.540

Sir. I have a proposition.



312

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:22.950

What is it?



313

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:28.500

Eren's Titan ability includes

too many uncertainties



314

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.290

which pose an ever-present danger.



315

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.950

As such, we will place Eren

under Captain Levi's supervision



316

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:36.870

and conduct a recon

mission outside the wall.



317

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:39.160

With Eren accompanying you?



318

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:40.250

Yes, Sir.



319

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:43.950

Based on the results of said mission,



320

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:47.580

you can decide if Eren

has control over his Titan ability



321

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:50.290

and if his existence

is of benefit to humankind.



322

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:53.790

Supervising Eren Jaeger, huh...



323

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:56.700

Can you do this, Levi?



324

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:59.580

Oh, I can most definitely kill him.



325

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:03.870

The <i>real </i>problem is

that there's no middle ground.



326

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.290

I've reached my decision.



327

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.910

Man, talk about harsh...



328

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.330

--I bet it hurts.

--A little...



329

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:24.660

--So, how exactly does it hurt?

--Huh?



330

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:26.540

I'm sorry about that.



331

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:30.200

But it <i>did </i>get you placed in our custody.



332

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:31.620

Yes...



333

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.200

The pain was worth it.



334

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:37.370

It let us play our trump card

when it would be most effective.



335

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:40.950

You have my admiration.



336

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:45.080

Eren. I look forward to working with you.



337

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:47.830

R-Right! Thank you, Sir!



338

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:51.290

Tell me, Eren.



339

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.160

Y-Yes?



340

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:54.790

Do you resent me?



341

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:56.370

N-No.



342

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.200

I understand it was

a necessary performance.



343

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:00.330

Good, then.



344

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:03.120

Still, you didn't have to go so far.



345

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:05.540

You knocked his tooth out!



346

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:08.250

--See?

--Don't pick that up. It's disgusting.



347

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:10.660

This is a precious sample of its own.



348

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:14.620

Eren. Be thankful you aren't

getting dissected by people like her.



349

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:17.160

Don't compare me with them.



350

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:20.290

I would never kill Eren.



351

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:24.080

Hey, Eren. Let me

see inside your mouth.



352

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.700

The tooth...



353

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:35.370

...has already grown back...



354

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:57.700

<i>If, by chance, I'm not me</i>



355

00:22:57.700 --> 00:23:02.950

<i>then who's to say that you're you?</i>



356

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:08.250

<i>Can you pick up the pieces of your heart</i>



357

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:13.370

<i>that fell apart like a broken sand castle?</i>



358

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:18.370

<i>The voice of someone calling out</i>



359

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:22.450

<i>changed into ringing in my ears</i>



360

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:27.620

<i>It's as if time has stopped</i>



361

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:30.410

<i>Now wake up</i>



362

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:35.700

<i>I made my way out of the deep darkness</i>



363

00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:40.950

<i>I fled like a swift wind</i>



364

00:23:40.950 --> 00:23:48.450

<i>We used to be like living corpses,</i>



365

00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:50.500

<i>but now we head beyond the walls</i>



366

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:52.540

<i>Let's meet again</i>



367

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:57.370

<i>in a place not on any map</i>



368

00:24:09.660 --> 00:24:14.120

After achieving his dream

of joining the Scout Regiment,



369

00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:16.910

Eren discovers that the Scouts

are a band of people



370

00:24:16.910 --> 00:24:21.000

who seek change, as well as a haven

of eccentrics and oddballs.



371

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.410

"Special Operations Squad"

"Eve of the Counterattack, Part 2"

